 ```
+
+
+### Plugin mission updates
+
+Deploy migration `missions.0009_mission_revision` with the revision-aware browser
+and plugin API. Reload open planner pages after deployment. Existing missions
+start at revision 1; browser saves and dashboard renames increment it.
+
+`GET /api/missions/<id>/` returns the mission revision. A token-authenticated
+`PATCH` to that URL must include the loaded `revision` and the mission payload.
+The server atomically checks and increments the revision, returning HTTP 409
+without changing the mission when it is stale or missing. Updates are scoped to
+the token owner and preserve settings omitted by the plugin. Reversed routes
+are rejected because the plugin cannot represent them. `POST /api/missions/`
+continues to create a new mission for Save as new and older plugin versions.
+
+The plugin remembers the link during its session. Conflicts offer Load latest
+(with a discard confirmation), Save as new, or Cancel. Browser autosave stops
+on conflicts and offers the same resolution choices. No automatic overwrite or
+merge is performed. Apply with `python manage.py migrate`; normal static asset
+deployment must include the updated planner JavaScript.
